  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific Audience Chamber/Arz Odasi on way103907818: enclosed pale chamber, real front doorway/closed rear door and recessed two-level windows; surrounding open round-arched colonnade with grey stone shafts/pale capitals/gold collars, low open balustrade, raised occupied podium/front steps and a broad shallow lead hip canopy with geometric coffered soffit. Preserve Gate of Felicity and other independent palace members. No copied tughra/calligraphy/floral ceiling art, furnishings, visitors or surveyed interior layout.",
    "identityBasis": "Audience Chamber member of Topkapi Q170495, OSM way103907818/native35184475996650. Native parent is the approximately31.4x29.2m canopy footprint with chamfered rear corners. Internal+X follows its long front elevation southeast; internal+Z faces southwest toward the separate Gate of Felicity. World heading0/native+X east,+Z south. Two ordinary exterior photos inspected; column/arch/door/canopy treatment is specific to this chamber.",
    "heightBasis": "No qualified native architectural height. Picture-led podium1.2m above front reference, shaft/capital/arch spring near6.6m, arcade crown8.2m, soffit8.9m and low hip roof near10.8m. Enclosed chamber21x16.2m and22 working column positions/eight front-row columns are footprint/photo-led visualization controls, not verified dimensions or inventory. Fine capitals, roof plan, painted art and hidden interior arrangement remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Original standard PMTiles/Mapzen terrain retained. Open front court internal[0,16] supplies providerY0. Occupied podium is level atY1.2 with foundations extending below original boundary minima; only the actual podium/front steps cut ground. No courtyard flattening or precinct slab. Original ground falls several metres beneath the east/rear side, so the protective foundation may be exposed there; that extension accommodates coarse terrain and does not assert historic retaining-wall height. Native exterior fit remains draft until rendered inspection; historical thresholds/accessibility need better ground data.",
